	(text "INPUT BUTTON ON A JUMPER-PICKED EF LINE, RUN AND LOAD, ONE DMA IN PER PRESS, Q LED" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 15.24 12.7 0) (effects (font (size 2.5 2.5) (bold yes)) (justify left top)) (uuid "395c621c-7b2c-5c49-8f78-39b0cfa9b315"))
	(text "INPUT (SW9, R1/C1 + Schmitt) drives EFOUT (open collector, U9A) to JP3: a jumper across a row puts it on -EF1, -EF2,\n-EF3 or -EF (set to -EF1); RN1 holds EFOUT high with no jumper. SW10 RUN/RESET grounds -RESET, SW11 LOAD grounds\n-PAUSE: both = LOAD mode (LOAD_H). In LOAD mode a press sets REQ (U10A); -DMAIN = NAND(REQ, SC0) (U9B, open drain):\nthe 1802 samples its DMA request at clock 7 of every cycle, before -MWR rises, so SC0, low from the start of the DMA\ncycle, lets the line go there (2026-11-22; REQ alone made two cycles of a press). The write's -MWR rise sets ACK\n(U10B), which clears REQ until the button is let go. DRIVE (U11A) keeps the switches on the bus until -MRD falls.\nThe Q LED sinks into U5B = NAND(Q, 1, 1), push-pull." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 15.24 17.78 0) (effects (font (size 1.5 1.5)) (justify left top)) (uuid "a288d6aa-5a72-519f-ad25-14c29c0743d2"))
	(embedded_fonts no)
)
